{"_notes":["Locally added -- upstream pinmame-nvram-maps has no map for NBA.","Built from a 4-player game driven through the cabinet's own streamer.","current_player and current_ball are adjacent in CPU RAM at 0x00033020 and 0x00033021, player low","and ball high. Scores are 4 bytes on 8-byte centres from 0x021109E4.","Nine records from 0x021029F8, bounded by where the 16-bit checksum stops validating -- the tenth","does not pass. Five are the high score ladder; four are champions, named off the machine's","post-game DMD cycle and each pinned by a distinct factory default: Free Throws 2 in a row,","2-Pointers 4, 3-Pointers 3, NBA Finals 25,000,000.","The machine displays a Basketball Points champion, and it is deliberately not mapped: it does not","appear to be stored as a champion record at all. Earning it (6 points) and exiting changed nothing","in the record block, put no 6 anywhere in the persistent region, and left record ten still failing","its checksum. Every persistent byte that did change has the audit shape -- a value written twice","followed by a checksum byte -- and the only 6s are in the volatile working area at 0x02111Axx,","among values that move by millions between captures. It reads as a per-game statistic the","game-over summary shows, not a persisted champion.","Score slots confirmed on that game: 1,336,840 for player 1 at 0x021109E4.","Only nba_802 is claimed; SAM addresses move between revisions.","game_over, tilted and credits come from a 1,099-frame recording of live memory spanning an","indices 30 and 32 as the free_play-relative rule predicted.","This ROM does not keep the ball+0x31 status byte its siblings use (a constant 0 here). Its game","state lives in a block at the top of RAM, 0x0003FF00-0x0003FFFF.","game_over at 0x0003FF83 reads 1 in the attract on both sides of the game and 0 in play, dropping","at the exact frame the game started -- the same frame credits fell -- and returning on the","frame of the last score change (the end-of-ball bonus). Correct in all 1,099 frames; any","non-zero value is game over, so no mask is needed. Ten neighbouring bytes carry the same edges.","tilted at 0x0003FF6B reads 4 for exactly the sixteen samples from the tilt to the end of the","tilted ball -- during which player 1's score sat frozen at 5,250 -- and 0 everywhere else in the","recording. Any non-zero value is tilted.","credits at 0x0211100C, the fourteenth SAM game at that address: rose to 9 with the coins (capped","by the Maximum Credits just set) and fell to 8 at game start.","2026-11: game_over and tilted read the status byte 0x00033052 (player + 0x32; 01 attract, 26","ball served, 12 play, 2F/66 modes, 14 tilted). On a cabinet the previous game_over 0x0003FF83","read game over for 6 s after the tilted ball drained, and tilted 0x0003FF6B went to 4 at each","ball launch, never at the tilt.","2026-11: The A.1 (63) and A.2 (33) adjustments added from the ROM image (README, 'Adjustments","from the ROM').","Confirmed on a cabinet 2026-11-13 (ALP4K; two players, tilt on P1 ball 1): 1,219,840 /","1,045,260, the records and the status byte matched the DMD."],"_fileformat":0.9,"_metadata":{"version":11,"license":"Open Data Commons Open Database License (ODbL) v1.0","copyright":["Copyright (C) 2026 by Wes Smith <evilwraith@gmail.com>"],"platform":"stern-sam.6e326d93","roms":["nba_802"],"validation":{"checksum":[{"_notes":"96 adjustments: 4-byte LE value, 1-byte checksum, 3 bytes 0xFF padding","label":"Adjustment {#} (checksum)","start":"0x02102008","length":5,"complement":true,"repeat":{"count":96,"step":8}},{"label":"Master Volume","start":"0x211024C","end":"0x211024D","complement":true},{"label":"Champion record {#} (checksum)","start":"0x21029F8","repeat":{"count":9,"step":32},"length":30,"bits":16,"complement":true}]},"values":{"no_yes":["NO","YES"],"credit_ticket_token":["CREDIT","TICKET","TOKEN"],"easy_medium_hard":["EASY","MEDIUM","HARD"]}},"checksum8":[{"label":"Free Play adjustment","start":"0x02102110","